<p>A federal judge in Washington ruled on Friday that parts of a Pentagon press access policy were unconstitutional, siding with The New York Times in its challenge to rules that withdrew or restricted credentials for several prominent news organizations. The court said those provisions violated the First and Fifth Amendments, rejecting the government’s argument that the measures were reasonable and necessary for national security.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/EBheTKop97DC6zGk7zzgYEQe-UXEspnMWiO9orBYLpJGs36BWXZcTdy91p8Ahf6LgEzvLdgZdFOMONulz5LVRYUzGMxBnfbAHRqF4Q3CiX87QjQHZbLZ9R-QonbXtEaED_uuiQg4qzFGFpMRYzJMwOJhbcZ_z1lXmHCbLD2dqwra2A8' alt='US Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth departs a press briefing on continued military operations at the Pentagon in Arlington, Virginia, on March 19, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Targeted press corps: Judge Paul Friedman said the Trump administration was trying to push out “disfavoured journalists,” suggesting the policy was more than a neutral access rule.</li><li>Wartime context: The ruling stressed the public’s need for information from multiple outlets while the United States is involved in a war with Iran and after its recent intervention in Venezuela.</li><li>Broad resistance: The policy drew pushback from US and international news organizations, with AFP, AP and Fox News among the outlets that declined to sign.</li><li>Judicial limit: The decision shows that courts can limit how far executive branch officials go in reshaping the Pentagon press corps through access rules.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>US government: The government said the Pentagon policy was reasonable and necessary to protect national security. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-judge-blocks-restrictive-pentagon-press-access-policy/article70768241.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Judge Paul Friedman: He said the public should be able to receive information from different perspectives and ruled that the challenged parts of the policy violated constitutional protections. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/20/us-judge-sides-with-new-york-times-against-pentagon-journalism-policies'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>The New York Times: The newspaper filed the lawsuit that led to the ruling, directly challenging the Pentagon’s restrictions on media access. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3347398/us-judge-rules-restrictive-pentagon-press-access-unconstitutional'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3347398/us-judge-rules-restrictive-pentagon-press-access-unconstitutional'>US judge rules restrictive Pentagon press access unconstitutional</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-judge-blocks-restrictive-pentagon-press-access-policy/article70768241.ece'>U.S. judge blocks restrictive Pentagon press access policy</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/21/us-judge-rules-pentagon-press-restrictions-unconstitutional_6751665_4.html'>US judge rules Pentagon press restrictions unconstitutional</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/20/us-judge-sides-with-new-york-times-against-pentagon-journalism-policies'>US judge sides with New York Times against Pentagon journalism policies</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/pentagons-limits-on-press-access-unconstitutional-us-judge-rules'>Pentagon’s limits on press access unconstitutional, US judge rules</a> - straitstimes.com</li></ul>